Source Review Evidence 1.0.0 — licence scope

Different components of this distribution have different terms. The scope
below and LICENSING_MAP.json identify the applicable component licences.
Copyright (c) 2026 Antonio Clim for his own material, except where an existing
notice identifies another holder. All existing notices remain in effect.

CODE — MIT

Author-controlled programme code, browser source, helpers, tests, functional
configuration and historical code snapshots are licensed under MIT. The same
terms apply to the author's code quoted in JSON, JSONL, logs, documentation
or patches. The complete terms are in LICENSES/MIT.txt. Preserve all applicable
copyright and permission notices, including the original CodeProbe
contributors notice retained in source/LICENSE and its historical copy.

DOCUMENTATION, FIGURES AND RESEARCH RECORDS — CC BY 4.0

Author-controlled distribution documentation, included figures, constructed
inputs, computational records and collection/database rights are licensed
under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International, to the extent of the
copyright and similar rights the author is entitled to grant. The complete
terms are in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt and at
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/legalcode.en.

Attribute this material to Antonio Clim, Source Review Evidence, version
1.0.0, retain the supplied provenance and indicate modifications. No exclusive
copyright is asserted in bare facts. Existing MIT-covered documentation
remains available under its existing MIT permission; this notice does not
withdraw or narrow that permission.

EXCEPTIONS AND MIXED MATERIAL

1. Existing licence and attribution notices retain their original terms.
2. SPDX documents declaring dataLicense: CC0-1.0 retain CC0 for their metadata
   only. This does not license the software or research material they describe.
3. Code and record portions retain their separate terms. CC BY for a record
   does not relicense code, a third-party extract or an original notice inside it.
4. Third-party material retains its own terms. References to dependencies,
   runtimes or comparator tools do not grant rights over their implementations.
   A component's external availability is separate from this distribution.
5. The manuscript, OR1, original OR2 archive and publisher materials are not
   included in this new distribution licence. They are not licensed for public
   redistribution by their mention in the provenance.

See docs/COMPONENT_RIGHTS.md and LICENSING_MAP.json for the component scope.
The licence texts themselves remain the unmodified standard terms; this
scope notice does not add restrictions to them or remove prior permissions.
